[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2601672849","pull_request_review_id":3556198478,"id":2601672849,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6bEmCR","diff_hunk":"@@ -573,7 +582,7 @@\n                 },\n                 {\n                     \"name\": \"p_argument_count\",\n-                    \"type\": \"int\"\n+                    \"type\": \"int32_t\"","path":"core/extension/gdextension_interface.json","commit_id":"6e6558c04b55764fbf8ea45ac4f078ea581e3770","original_commit_id":"6e6558c04b55764fbf8ea45ac4f078ea581e3770","user":{"login":"touilleMan","id":3187637,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODc2Mzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3187637?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan","html_url":"https://github.com/touilleMan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Since in C `int` and `int32_t` are not strictly equivalent, does this mean the underlying data type has been changed to actually use `int32_t` type ?\r\n\r\nI guess in practice this might not be a real concern, since most (all ?) modern platform store `int` on 4 bytes anyway, however we might have some issues if some lunatic decide do export his game to a 16bits processor :smile: \r\n\r\n(and if the type is changed, shouldn't we use `uint32_t` given a negative argument count is meaningless ? :thinking: )","created_at":"2025-12-09T08:54:34Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T08:54:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113754#discussion_r2601672849","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113754","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2601672849"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113754#discussion_r2601672849"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113754"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2601672849/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":585,"original_line":585,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":100,"position":100,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2602374812","pull_request_review_id":3557080474,"id":2602374812,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6bHRac","diff_hunk":"@@ -573,7 +582,7 @@\n                 },\n                 {\n                     \"name\": \"p_argument_count\",\n-                    \"type\": \"int\"\n+                    \"type\": \"int32_t\"","path":"core/extension/gdextension_interface.json","commit_id":"6e6558c04b55764fbf8ea45ac4f078ea581e3770","original_commit_id":"6e6558c04b55764fbf8ea45ac4f078ea581e3770","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> Since in C `int` and `int32_t` are not strictly equivalent, does this mean the underlying data type has been changed to actually use `int32_t` type ?\r\n\r\nOn all the platforms/compiler that we currently support, `int` is a 32-bit integer and so effectively the same as `int32_t`. So, I don't really think of this as changing anything, but just making the size explicit and not potentially up to interpretation\r\n\r\n> (and if the type is changed, shouldn't we use `uint32_t` given a negative argument count is meaningless ? 🤔 )\r\n\r\nI'd really prefer to change as little as possible now that we're after the feature freeze\r\n\r\nPerhaps we could change this in the 4.7 dev cycle? And if we do so, also update all the actual functions these function pointers are for (which are in `variant_call.cpp` and currently use `int` for the argument count)","created_at":"2025-12-09T12:09:25Z","updated_at":"2025-12-09T12:09:25Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113754#discussion_r2602374812","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113754","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2602374812"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113754#discussion_r2602374812"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113754"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2602374812/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":585,"original_line":585,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2601672849,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":100,"position":100,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2602417263","pull_request_review_id":3557133240,"id":2602417263,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6bHbxv","diff_hunk":"@@ -573,7 +582,7 @@\n                 },\n                 {\n                     \"name\": \"p_argument_count\",\n-                    \"type\": \"int\"\n+                    \"type\": \"int32_t\"","path":"core/extension/gdextension_interface.json","commit_id":"6e6558c04b55764fbf8ea45ac4f078ea581e3770","original_commit_id":"6e6558c04b55764fbf8ea45ac4f078ea581e3770","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Yes, I agree to postpone other consistency issues. Changing signed -> unsigned is technically a binary breaking change, even though it matters only for negative / very high unsigned values. But having a full dev cycle to see if this may cause problems is probably safer.","crea